  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Consider an array AAA consisting of NNN positive elements. The frequency array of AAA is the array BBB of size NNN such that Bi=B_i =Bi​= frequency of element AiA_iAi​ in AAA.\n\nFor example, if A=[4,7,4,11,2,7,7]A = [4, 7, 4, 11, 2, 7, 7]A=[4,7,4,11,2,7,7], the frequency array B=[2,3,2,1,1,3,3]B = [2, 3, 2, 1, 1, 3, 3]B=[2,3,2,1,1,3,3].\n\nYou have lost the array AAA, but fortunately you have the array BBB.\n\nYour task is to construct the **lexicographically smallest** array AAA such that:\n\n\n1≤Ai≤1051\\le A_i \\le 10^51≤Ai​≤105;\nThe frequency array of AAA is equal to BBB.\nIf no such array AAA exists, print −1-1−1.\n\nNote: Array XXX is lexicographically smaller than array YYY, if Xi&lt;YiX_i \\lt Y_iXi​&lt;Yi​, where iii is the first index where XXX and YYY differ.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of two lines of input.\n\nThe first line of each test case contains a single integer NNN — the size of the array.\nThe next line contains NNN space-separated integers - B1,B2,…,BNB_1, B_2, \\ldots, B_NB1​,B2​,…,BN​, the frequency array.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a new line, NNN space separated integers - A1,A2,…,ANA_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_NA1​,A2​,…,AN​, the **lexicographically smallest** array AAA. If no such array AAA exists, print −1-1−1.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1051 \\leq T \\leq 10^51≤T≤105",
      "1≤N≤1051 \\leq N \\leq 10^51≤N≤105",
      "1≤Bi≤1051 \\leq B_i \\leq 10^51≤Bi​≤105",
      "The sum of NNN over all test cases won't exceed 10610^6106."
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
