        "input": "5\n5\n2 3 3 3 2\n5\n1 1 1 1 1\n5\n5 5 5 5 5\n3\n1 2 4\n8\n1 3 2 3 2 2 2 3",
        "output": "1 2 2 2 1\n1 2 3 4 5\n1 1 1 1 1\n-1\n1 2 3 2 3 4 4 2",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest case 111: The lexicographically smallest array AAA having the given frequency array BBB is A=[1,2,2,2,1]A = [1, 2, 2, 2, 1]A=[1,2,2,2,1]. The element A1A_1A1​ and A5A_5A5​ have frequency 222 while A2,A3,A_2, A_3,A2​,A3​, and A4A_4A4​ have frequency 333.\nTest case 222: The lexicographically smallest array AAA having the given frequency array BBB is A=[1,2,3,4,5]A = [1, 2, 3, 4, 5]A=[1,2,3,4,5]. Each element in AAA has frequency 111.\nTest case 333: The lexicographically smallest array AAA having the given frequency array BBB is A=[1,1,1,1,1]A = [1, 1, 1, 1, 1]A=[1,1,1,1,1]. Each element in AAA has frequency 555.\nTest case 444: No possible array AAA exists having the given frequency array."
      }
